  count how many jelly beans are in a jar  but modern day voter suppression is no  less pernicious  yesterday i was honored to join  president biden and vice president  harris and our madam  leader of the congressional black caucus  joyce baby  as the president spoke of an urgent need  to protect the sacred right to vote i  applaud the president for being  unequivocal  in his statement that by any means  necessary we must  change the rules of the senate and pass  the john robert lewis voting rights act  our nation is at an inflection point  voting right legislation will go to the  senate floor and it must pass  you know we're on the anniversary the  cusp of  the martin luther king celebration day  monday  but there can be no celebration  without liberation  without freedom  without the right to vote  as we prepare to observe the birthday of  reverend dr martin luther king let us  remember that just as delayed can be  just as denied  the time to act is now nothing is more  fundamental to our democracy than the  sacred right to vote  the time to talk is over  it's now time to act  my name is colin allred  represent texas's 32nd district i'm  proud to be here  my colleagues in the congressional black  caucus but i'm also a former voting  rights lawyer  i can tell you  we knew  when we'd go into court there'd be some  judges that we weren't going to get a  good ruling from  we knew that  the courts might not be on our side  we always had  the law  we have the voting rights act  we don't have that protection right now  and we know that it's not going to be  the courts that are going to protect our  rights  right now  it's going to have to be us in the  congress  and so the congressional black caucus is  coming together today  to say to the united states senate  there is nothing more important  after our capital was attacked by people  trying to overthrow our democracy  after a rash of laws have passed across  this country to try and make it harder  for certain americans to vote  in the state of texas where it was  already the hardest state in the country  to vote they just went and made it  harder  that now is the time to act  that believe us  believe us when we tell you i've spoken  to voters who've been disenfranchised i  can see the light go out of their eyes  the belief in our democracy leave them  we have to restore our democracy and  this is the time  we cannot let a senate rule  a senate rule that is based and was used  almost exclusively to prevent civil  rights  prevent us from rising to this moment i  know all of us in the congressional  black caucus will do everything we can  but we're calling on the united states  senate  we're calling on a few senators in  particular  to rise to this moment  pass your own bill senator  pass the john lewis voting rights  advancement act give us the tools to  rescue our democracy and let us let the  chips fall where they may in the next  elections  thank you  val demings representing florida's  10th congressional district we are the  home of the brave land of the free  the greatest nation  in the world  but we are here today to hold america  to its promise  i stand today remembering my parents  my father was a janitor and my mother  a  maid my dad used to go to work seven  days a week to make ends meet  for our family but i cannot remember a  time  that my parents  did not pass  their vote they saw it as their  civic  duty  my parents understood that their vote  while they didn't have enough a lot of  money their name was on no buildings  their name wasn't famous people didn't  rise when they walked into the room that  their vote mattered  and it mattered just as much as the  richest man  or woman in town we can talk about  health care we can talk about civil  rights we can talk about women's rights  we can talk about social security  medicare education  but all of it is at risk  all of it  everything that you care about  regardless of your party and everything  that we care about is at 